<title>BELGIUM: EU praises sustainability of German deficit cuts.</title>
<headline>EU praises sustainability of German deficit cuts.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission on Monday applauded Germany for cutting its budget deficit by means of structural measures that would remain in place over the long-term.  </p>
<p>The Commission comment came in a recommendation to finance ministers who were expected later on Monday to rubber-stamp them.</p>
<p>&quot;(The EU) acknowledges that the reduction of the government deficit from 3.8 percent of GDP in 1996 to 2.9 percent in 1997 constitutes a major effort as it relies mainly on structural measures with positive implications for the longer-term sustainability of the consolidation,&quot; the recommendation said.</p>
</text>
